      "cause": "1.2M keys written by one warm-up job with the same TTL all expired in the same second",
      "why": "The warmer SETs every product with EX 3600, so the whole keyspace expires together an hour later. Every request then misses at once, each miss goes to Postgres, and concurrent misses for the same key aren’t coalesced — the DB runs out of connections before the cache can refill.",
